'''Costarruga''' ({{Literal translation|rough coast|wrinkled coast}}; {{Langx|arn|Pangalafken|4=puma coast}}; {{Langx|huh|Püñehuel|4=pointed place}}) is one of ten regions of [[Hesperia]], within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. It is bordered by [[Arcadia]] and [[Cadaqués]] to the north and northwest, [[Acacias]] to the southeast, and [[Trás-as-Montanyas]] to the southwest. It has an area of {{convert|49763.88|km2|abbr=on}} making it the 37th largest region of Balisca. 

It had an estimated population of 2,067,648 in 2023. The capital and largest city is [[Curicó]].

